DECISIONS 278, 284: gen/ts writes a record value with its stored results, so a result holding its own receiver is a literal without end: RecordCycleThroughMethod once, at the fn, from check, not a stack overflow of the build.
-- a/a.canon --
package a

/// A tone.
enum Tone { soft, loud }

/// A thing.
record Thing {
  /// Its key.
  a: Int
  /// Itself, per tone.
  export fn me(self, t: Tone) -> Thing { return self }
}

/// The things.
let things: [Thing] keyed by a = [{ a: 1 }]

emit ts { out: "@features/a/a.ts" }
-- findings.txt --
error[E8019]  a/a.canon:11:13
  emit ts in baked mode cannot generate a by-value cycle of records through a stored method result; return a ref to the record instead

1 error, 0 warnings in 1 package (…)
